  <revision rev="12" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>8bc1b0b423d809e95ccc3f1a79fb66f3</srcmd5>
    <version>0.14.0</version>
    <time>1787566240</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update python-SoundFile to 0.14.0.

- Upstream adds type annotations across the public API, fixes a race
  condition when opening files concurrently, fixes test-suite
  regressions and drops Python 3.9 and older (python_requires &gt;= 3.10).
- New mandatory runtime dependency python-typing_extensions: soundfile.py
  now does an unconditional &quot;from typing_extensions import Self&quot;.
- Dropped the openSUSE-only 0001-Fix-libsndfile-versioning.patch:
  openSUSE builds libsndfile without experimental code, so
  sf_version_string() returns &quot;libsndfile-1.2.2&quot; with no &quot;-exp&quot; suffix
  to strip (verified on a current system).
- Still noarch cffi ABI mode: soundfile_build.py is byte-identical to
  0.13.1, so no libsndfile floor change and no bundled library.

Built locally with osc build --clean for openSUSE_Tumbleweed/aarch64:
python313 and python314 flavors, tests 330 passed / 1 deselected
(test_write_mp3_compression, openSUSE libsndfile has no MPEG),
rpmlint 0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 badness.</comment>
    <requestid>1373168</requestid>
  </revision>
